260
00:25:56.935 --> 00:25:58.312
Go watch your brother, okay?

261
00:26:01.148 --> 00:26:03.275
Garrett?

262
00:26:06.153 --> 00:26:08.697
Garrett!

263
00:26:24.672 --> 00:26:26.632
What is this?

264
00:26:28.550 --> 00:26:31.345
Who are you?

265
00:26:31.387 --> 00:26:33.138
That car.

266
00:26:33.180 --> 00:26:35.808
Did you see that car?
You see what happened?

267
00:26:42.231 --> 00:26:44.983
Did you see who took my brother?

268
00:26:46.735 --> 00:26:47.820
Wait! No.

269
00:27:23.689 --> 00:27:26.859
- Hey.
- Hey, Max.

270
00:27:32.531 --> 00:27:35.951
So? How'd it go?

271
00:27:37.244 --> 00:27:38.996
Uh...

272
00:27:39.038 --> 00:27:41.290
it was interesting.

273
00:27:41.331 --> 00:27:44.752
I should probably
get out of here.

274
00:27:44.793 --> 00:27:49.840
Hey, by the way, I-I do intend
on-on paying you, eventually.

275
00:27:49.882 --> 00:27:51.842
It's okay.

276
00:27:51.884 --> 00:27:53.552
I know where you live.

277
00:28:17.951 --> 00:28:19.411
Hey. Welcome to Sparky's.

278
00:28:19.453 --> 00:28:21.622
Could I set you folks up
with some appetizers?

279
00:28:21.663 --> 00:28:23.582
- Yes.
- Oh.

280
00:28:23.624 --> 00:28:25.042
We are not eating.

281
00:28:25.084 --> 00:28:26.752
Well, that's no fun.

282
00:28:26.794 --> 00:28:28.087
You do realize that lunch

283
00:28:28.128 --> 00:28:29.463
is the most important meal
of the day?

284
00:28:29.505 --> 00:28:31.632
I thought it was breakfast.

285
00:28:31.674 --> 00:28:33.217
Some people say that,

286
00:28:33.258 --> 00:28:35.052
- but, you know, it's just a theory.
- Are you being paid

287
00:28:35.094 --> 00:28:37.054
by the word,
or could we have a minute?

288
00:28:37.096 --> 00:28:39.807
- All right.
- Thank you.

289
00:28:39.848 --> 00:28:41.558
Ah, where were we?

290
00:28:41.600 --> 00:28:43.143
Oh, you were about to tell me

291
00:28:43.185 --> 00:28:44.311
what a miserable failure you are.

292
00:28:44.353 --> 00:28:46.563
Hey, screw you, lady.

293
00:28:46.605 --> 00:28:49.191
My sister went over every inch
of that dump a thousand times.

294
00:28:49.233 --> 00:28:52.569
If there was something to find,
she would have found it.

295
00:28:52.611 --> 00:28:54.029
Now pay up.

296
00:28:54.371 --> 00:28:56.907
- Uh, I'm sorry?
- You said 200.

297
00:28:56.948 --> 00:28:58.258
We had a deal.

298
00:28:58.260 --> 00:29:00.275
Yeah, that you were gonna find me

299
00:29:00.285 --> 00:29:03.038
hard proof of criminal endangerment.

300
00:29:03.080 --> 00:29:06.041
Instead, you've told me
what a nice kid my niece is

301
00:29:06.083 --> 00:29:08.043
and that my nephew sleeps a lot.

302
00:29:08.085 --> 00:29:09.420
He really does, though.

303
00:29:09.461 --> 00:29:12.031
Sleeping is not a crime.

304
00:29:13.173 --> 00:29:14.516
Is that guy okay?

305
00:29:14.658 --> 00:29:17.911
I just realized I shouldn't
be hearing any of this.

306
00:29:18.153 --> 00:29:20.389
As a matter of fact,
I shouldn't be here at all.

307
00:29:20.431 --> 00:29:21.890
Sit down, Doug.

308
00:29:23.017 --> 00:29:24.601
So, I guess we're finished here,

309
00:29:24.643 --> 00:29:27.429
unless either one of you
has a brilliant idea,

310
00:29:27.471 --> 00:29:29.848
which I realize is highly unlikely.

311
00:29:29.890 --> 00:29:31.767
Why don't we just kill him?

312
00:29:34.820 --> 00:29:37.281
Tempting. But no.

313
00:29:37.322 --> 00:29:40.617
- What else?
- Mike was saying that...

314
00:29:40.659 --> 00:29:44.955
he really needs this new job
to, like, look good on paper

315
00:29:44.997 --> 00:29:47.166
for the judge or something.

316
00:29:47.207 --> 00:29:48.709
Well, that's all
very fascinating, honey,

317
00:29:48.751 --> 00:29:50.961
but I am not hearing a plan.

318
00:29:51.837 --> 00:29:53.505
We toss the place.

319
00:29:54.340 --> 00:29:57.051
- Go on.
- Well, he's a security guard, right?

320
00:29:57.092 --> 00:29:59.928
His job is to make sure
nobody gets in.

321
00:29:59.970 --> 00:30:03.182
So, we get in,

322
00:30:03.223 --> 00:30:05.142
and we mess up the place good.

323
00:30:05.484 --> 00:30:07.603
We help ourselves to whatever
we find along the way.

324
00:30:07.944 --> 00:30:09.780
Your nephew gets canned.

325
00:30:09.781 --> 00:30:12.935
Judge gives you the kid,
and you give us...

326
00:30:13.016 --> 00:30:15.461
$2,000.

327
00:30:16.362 --> 00:30:18.113
One thousand.

328
00:30:18.906 --> 00:30:22.034
But do it fast,
and don't mess it up.

329
00:30:22.076 --> 00:30:23.535
I mean, you know, mess it up,

330
00:30:23.577 --> 00:30:26.580
but don't...
don't mess this up.

331
00:30:33.587 --> 00:30:36.131
Come on. <i></i>

332
00:30:36.173 --> 00:30:38.133
What are you doing?

333
00:30:42.054 --> 00:30:43.430
Abby, do you need something?

334
00:30:43.472 --> 00:30:45.140
- No.
- All right, quit playing and take that off.

335
00:30:45.182 --> 00:30:46.308
I have to go to work.

336
00:30:46.350 --> 00:30:48.018
I know. I'm coming with you.

337
00:30:48.060 --> 00:30:49.186
No, you're not.

338
00:30:49.228 --> 00:30:51.146
- Give me the vest.
- No.

339
00:30:51.188 --> 00:30:53.899
Give me the vest now.

340
00:30:53.941 --> 00:30:56.610
I'm coming with you.

341
00:30:56.652 --> 00:30:58.779
- I want to go with you.
- Abby.

342
00:30:58.821 --> 00:31:00.614
- I don't want to stay here with Max.
- Abby, stop.

343
00:31:00.656 --> 00:31:01.439
- Hello?
- Abby, stop.

344
00:31:01.449 --> 00:31:02.449
No! You can't make me.

345
00:31:02.491 --> 00:31:03.826
- Yes, I can.
- No, it's mine.

346
00:31:03.867 --> 00:31:05.035
- Hello?

347
00:31:05.077 --> 00:31:06.829
Let go!

348
00:31:06.870 --> 00:31:08.789
- Let go. No, no.
- Abby, stop. Abby.

349
00:31:08.831 --> 00:31:11.250
- He's taking my vest!
- Abby.

350
00:31:11.291 --> 00:31:12.751
- I'm keeping it.
- No.

351
00:31:15.921 --> 00:31:17.840
She's all yours.

352
00:32:19.151 --> 00:32:21.070
Garrett!

353
00:32:28.994 --> 00:32:30.245
Wait, please.

354
00:32:30.287 --> 00:32:33.582
Please don't-don't...
don't run.

355
00:32:33.624 --> 00:32:36.710
Okay? I-I just want to know
what you saw.

356
00:32:41.382 --> 00:32:44.468
Please. I'm begging you.

357
00:32:44.510 --> 00:32:46.303
Help me.

358
00:32:50.849 --> 00:32:52.601
Who took Garrett?!

359
00:33:23.298 --> 00:33:25.634
<i>♪ The secrets that you just can't hide... ♪</i>

360
00:33:28.721 --> 00:33:31.181
<i>♪ You tell me that you want me... ♪</i>

361
00:34:06.675 --> 00:34:08.052
About time.

362
00:34:08.093 --> 00:34:11.680
Starting to think maybe
you fell asleep on the job.

363
00:34:11.722 --> 00:34:12.890
Um...

364
00:34:12.931 --> 00:34:15.434
Can I, uh, help you, Officer?

365
00:34:15.476 --> 00:34:18.103
Please, my name's Vanessa.

366
00:34:18.145 --> 00:34:20.647
And you must be?

367
00:34:20.689 --> 00:34:22.566
Um...

368
00:34:22.608 --> 00:34:25.277
- The new security guard.
- Yeah.

369
00:34:26.862 --> 00:34:29.198
You're bleeding, by the way.

370
00:34:32.117 --> 00:34:34.536
Looks nasty.

371
00:34:34.578 --> 00:34:38.165
Come on. I know where they keep
the first aid kit.

372
00:34:48.634 --> 00:34:51.178
Love what
you've done with the place.

373
00:34:51.220 --> 00:34:53.097
Why Nebraska?

374
00:34:53.847 --> 00:34:56.684
- Oh, you need a hand?
- I'm fine.

375
00:34:57.810 --> 00:34:58.977
You sure?

376
00:34:59.019 --> 00:35:00.270
Here.

377
00:35:00.312 --> 00:35:02.106
I'm a certified EMT.

378
00:35:02.147 --> 00:35:05.693
So if your heart ever goes out,
I'm the one you want to call.

379
00:35:07.986 --> 00:35:10.072
You seem to really know
your way around the place.

380
00:35:10.114 --> 00:35:12.116
Well, Freddy's is on my beat.

381
00:35:12.157 --> 00:35:14.493
I like to stay well informed.

382
00:35:16.286 --> 00:35:19.331
Also, I really loved this place
as a kid.

383
00:35:22.710 --> 00:35:24.169
There.

384
00:35:24.211 --> 00:35:26.505
That should do it.

385
00:35:27.381 --> 00:35:29.341
Vanessa Shelly.

386
00:35:30.175 --> 00:35:31.593
Mike.

387
00:35:31.635 --> 00:35:33.846
Pleasure to meet you, Mike.

388
00:35:39.977 --> 00:35:42.855
You doing all right this evening, Mike?

389
00:35:44.565 --> 00:35:45.649
What?

390
00:35:45.691 --> 00:35:47.401
Are you good? Are you okay?

391
00:35:47.443 --> 00:35:48.944
Is everything copacetic?

392
00:35:48.986 --> 00:35:51.947
Yeah, I know what "all right" means.

393
00:35:51.989 --> 00:35:53.532
Do you also know that your eyes
are bloodshot

394
00:35:53.574 --> 00:35:54.950
and your heart rate's
through the roof?

395
00:35:54.992 --> 00:35:57.327
And aside from that gash
on your arm,

396
00:35:57.369 --> 00:35:58.996
which...
let's be honest,

397
00:35:59.038 --> 00:36:02.124
is pretty frickin' bizarre,
you've been acting suspicious

398
00:36:02.166 --> 00:36:03.876
since the moment you opened the door.

399
00:36:05.919 --> 00:36:09.673
Yeah, look, it's been a weird night.

400
00:36:14.053 --> 00:36:16.513
Sounds like Freddy's.

401
00:36:20.059 --> 00:36:22.227
This place, it gets to people.

402
00:36:22.978 --> 00:36:25.105
It's one of the reasons why
you're gonna quit.

403
00:36:25.147 --> 00:36:26.857
I'm sorry?

404
00:36:26.899 --> 00:36:27.983
Oh, yeah.

405
00:36:28.025 --> 00:36:30.903
You security hires, you never last.

406
00:36:34.573 --> 00:36:36.450
Have you met them yet?

407
00:36:38.077 --> 00:36:39.453
Met who?

408
00:36:45.250 --> 00:36:47.670
So, what are the other reasons?

409
00:36:47.711 --> 00:36:48.754
Huh?

410
00:36:48.796 --> 00:36:50.214
Why you think I'm gonna quit my job?

411
00:36:50.255 --> 00:36:51.507
Well, you tell me.

412
00:36:51.548 --> 00:36:53.550
Is this somewhere you see yourself

413
00:36:53.592 --> 00:36:55.636
10, 20 years from now?

414
00:36:55.978 --> 00:36:58.122
I mean, what do I know?
Maybe the benefits are great.

415
00:36:58.963 --> 00:37:00.633
I didn't think so.

416
00:37:00.974 --> 00:37:03.936
Add to that the thing
with those kids going missing.

417
00:37:06.105 --> 00:37:07.564
Wh-What did you just say?

418
00:37:07.606 --> 00:37:10.109
Prepare to have your mind blown.

419
00:37:26.458 --> 00:37:28.544
<i>♪ When you close your eyes ♪</i>

420
00:37:28.585 --> 00:37:29.920
<i>♪ And you go to sleep ♪</i>

421
00:37:29.962 --> 00:37:31.714
<i>♪ Sleep, sleep, sleep ♪</i>

422
00:37:33.257 --> 00:37:36.593
<i>♪ And it's down to the sound
of a heartbeat ♪</i>

423
00:37:36.635 --> 00:37:38.679
This... this is...

424
00:37:38.721 --> 00:37:41.098
The best thing you've seen
in your entire life?

425
00:37:41.140 --> 00:37:44.518
<i>♪ I can hear the things
that you're dreaming about ♪</i>

426
00:37:44.560 --> 00:37:46.520
<i>♪ About, about, about ♪</i>

427
00:37:48.313 --> 00:37:50.774
- <i>♪ When you open up your... ♪</i>
- Want to dance?

428
00:38:00.659 --> 00:38:02.494
Maybe some other time.

429
00:38:04.663 --> 00:38:08.292
Wait, y-you said
some kids went missing?

430
00:38:08.334 --> 00:38:10.586
Sure. Back in the '80s.

431
00:38:10.627 --> 00:38:11.920
What happened to them?

432
00:38:11.962 --> 00:38:14.298
It was big news.

433
00:38:14.340 --> 00:38:16.508
That's why the place shut down.

434
00:38:17.301 --> 00:38:18.677
Wow.

435
00:38:18.719 --> 00:38:20.721
You really didn't do
your homework, did you?

436
00:38:21.638 --> 00:38:25.017
And you're not even
wearing your badge.

437
00:38:26.352 --> 00:38:28.562
Got it.

438
00:38:34.735 --> 00:38:36.111
There.

439
00:38:36.153 --> 00:38:38.655
Now you're official.

440
00:38:44.370 --> 00:38:46.497
Hey.

441
00:38:46.538 --> 00:38:47.831
Some friendly advice?

442
00:38:47.873 --> 00:38:50.417
Don't let this place get to you.

443
00:38:50.459 --> 00:38:53.045
Just do your job, and you'll be fine.

444
00:38:56.507 --> 00:38:58.050
Yeah, sounds good.

445
00:39:21.073 --> 00:39:23.033
<i>It's showtime.<i>

446
00:39:23.075 --> 00:39:26.662
As soon as he gets back,
get the guys and meet me here.

447
00:39:26.704 --> 00:39:30.082
I think I see a way in.

448
00:39:43.262 --> 00:39:45.472
All right.

449
00:39:45.514 --> 00:39:47.725
Now, be quick but thorough.

450
00:39:47.766 --> 00:39:50.102
Maximum damage, minimum time.

451
00:39:51.937 --> 00:39:53.814
You see anything valuable,
grab it,

452
00:39:53.856 --> 00:39:55.899
and we'll, uh, settle up after.

453
00:39:55.941 --> 00:39:57.735
- Good?
- Yeah. Golden.

454
00:39:57.776 --> 00:39:59.570
- Whoo!
- Yeah!

455
00:39:59.611 --> 00:40:01.113
- Let's go, boys!
- Come on!

456
00:41:51.473 --> 00:41:52.725
Carl?

457
00:42:16.874 --> 00:42:18.125
Hank?

458
00:42:19.084 --> 00:42:21.462
What the hell are you doing?

459
00:42:30.012 --> 00:42:32.264
Hank?

460
00:42:32.306 --> 00:42:33.515
- Hank!
- Jeff?

461
00:42:35.768 --> 00:42:36.977
Jeff!

462
00:42:39.563 --> 00:42:40.647
Come on, you stupid...

463
00:42:40.689 --> 00:42:41.940
Hank?

464
00:42:43.025 --> 00:42:45.277
Come on. Come on.

465
00:43:08.258 --> 00:43:09.718
Hank?

466
00:43:59.059 --> 00:44:00.811
Shit.

467
00:44:06.859 --> 00:44:10.195
No! No! No!

468
00:45:11.757 --> 00:45:13.759
Jeff?

469
00:45:15.469 --> 00:45:16.679
Carl?

470
00:45:23.644 --> 00:45:24.853
Hey.

471
00:45:24.895 --> 00:45:26.605
Follow me.

472
00:45:26.647 --> 00:45:28.816
Hey!

473
00:45:28.857 --> 00:45:29.900
Hey, wait!

474
00:45:29.942 --> 00:45:32.194
Come on.

475
00:45:35.114 --> 00:45:36.782
Hello?

476
00:45:41.412 --> 00:45:43.789
This way.

477
00:46:11.483 --> 00:46:13.360
Warmer.

478
00:46:17.614 --> 00:46:20.993
How in the heck?

479
00:46:25.998 --> 00:46:28.000
Warmer.

480
00:46:59.323 --> 00:47:02.659
It's feeding
time for the giraffe.

481
00:47:09.958 --> 00:47:12.461
Hey, Abs, what you working on?

482
00:47:15.756 --> 00:47:17.049
All right.

483
00:47:17.091 --> 00:47:19.885
I guess you don't want this, then.

484
00:47:24.973 --> 00:47:26.892
It's cool, huh?

485
00:47:31.939 --> 00:47:34.066
Okay.

486
00:47:40.280 --> 00:47:42.366
I'm trying my best, Abby, okay?

487
00:48:02.219 --> 00:48:03.721
<i>Can't you read?</i>

488
00:48:03.762 --> 00:48:06.265
You okay?

489
00:48:07.558 --> 00:48:10.060
I made a mess.

490
00:48:10.102 --> 00:48:11.687
I'm sorry.

491
00:48:12.604 --> 00:48:15.190
They're just...
they're just papers, all right?

492
00:48:15.232 --> 00:48:17.109
They don't...
they don't mean anything.

493
00:48:17.151 --> 00:48:19.236
Then why do you have them?

494
00:48:19.278 --> 00:48:22.031
Well, that's complicated.
Aunt Jane...

495
00:48:22.072 --> 00:48:23.407
I hate her.

496
00:48:23.449 --> 00:48:25.743
She's mean and she smells
like cigarettes.

497
00:48:27.494 --> 00:48:28.996
It's not funny.

498
00:48:29.038 --> 00:48:31.248
You're right, it's not.
It's just, uh...

499
00:48:31.290 --> 00:48:32.875
I don't know, it's nice that

500
00:48:32.916 --> 00:48:35.210
we can finally agree
about something.

501
00:48:35.252 --> 00:48:38.005
Are you gonna
give me away?

502
00:48:38.047 --> 00:48:40.299
Abs, no, I...

503
00:48:45.179 --> 00:48:46.472
Hey. Vanessa.

504
00:48:46.513 --> 00:48:48.140
Hey, Mike.

505
00:48:48.182 --> 00:48:50.017
And hello.

506
00:48:50.059 --> 00:48:52.686
Vanessa, this is Abby.
Abby, Vanessa.

507
00:48:52.728 --> 00:48:55.189
Hi, Abby.

508
00:48:55.230 --> 00:48:57.649
Mike didn't tell me
he had a daughter.

509
00:48:57.691 --> 00:48:59.568
- Gross.
- No, uh, Abby's my sister.

510
00:48:59.610 --> 00:49:02.905
Ah. Well, he didn't tell me
he had a sister either.

511
00:49:02.946 --> 00:49:05.449
Are you here to arrest Mike?

512
00:49:05.491 --> 00:49:07.701
Okay, uh, can you
go play in your room

513
00:49:07.743 --> 00:49:09.745
so me and Vanessa can talk?

514
00:49:09.787 --> 00:49:11.163
It's nice to meet you.

515
00:49:12.998 --> 00:49:16.126
What, um...
what are you doing here?

516
00:49:16.168 --> 00:49:18.962
- Somebody broke into Freddy's.
- What?

517
00:49:19.004 --> 00:49:20.881
Wh-What-what happened?

518
00:49:20.923 --> 00:49:23.258
Recognize these?

519
00:49:24.677 --> 00:49:26.345
Look, it's not
what you think, okay?

520
00:49:26.387 --> 00:49:28.305
Th-Those are--
They're sleeping pills.

521
00:49:28.347 --> 00:49:30.015
- They help me sleep.
- I know what they are, Mike.

522
00:49:30.057 --> 00:49:31.350
It's written on the bottle.

523
00:49:32.685 --> 00:49:34.645
News flash...
If you're too whacked out

524
00:49:34.687 --> 00:49:36.188
to remember to lock
a friggin' door,

525
00:49:36.230 --> 00:49:38.399
accident or not, you're liable.

526
00:49:38.440 --> 00:49:40.234
It's called criminal negligence.

527
00:49:40.275 --> 00:49:42.653
You wouldn't understand.

528
00:49:42.695 --> 00:49:44.196
Well, then help me.

529
00:49:44.238 --> 00:49:46.240
'Cause the moment I file that report,

530
00:49:46.281 --> 00:49:49.034
it's out of my hands.

531
00:49:53.038 --> 00:49:55.374
You want to take a walk?

532
00:49:59.044 --> 00:50:01.755
So I used to have a brother.

533
00:50:04.008 --> 00:50:06.051
His name was Garrett.

534
00:50:07.386 --> 00:50:09.847
And when I was...

535
00:50:09.888 --> 00:50:12.349
about 12,

536
00:50:12.391 --> 00:50:14.768
he was, uh, he was taken.

537
00:50:16.145 --> 00:50:18.480
And I was there when it happened.

538
00:50:20.315 --> 00:50:22.026
They never found the guy who did it,

539
00:50:22.067 --> 00:50:23.652
and they never found my brother.

540
00:50:28.866 --> 00:50:32.995
So there's this theory that,
uh, we can't forget things.

541
00:50:33.037 --> 00:50:35.998
Basically, it says that
every single thing that you see

542
00:50:36.040 --> 00:50:38.792
in your entire life,
down to the tiniest of details,

543
00:50:38.834 --> 00:50:40.711
gets stored inside of you.

544
00:50:40.753 --> 00:50:44.048
You just have to know how to look.

545
00:50:44.089 --> 00:50:46.216
Your brother-

546
00:50:46.258 --> 00:50:48.344
you think you saw who took him?

547
00:50:48.385 --> 00:50:50.346
I know I did.

548
00:50:50.387 --> 00:50:52.848
And I know that he's in here,
but he's just- he's-

549
00:50:52.890 --> 00:50:54.058
It's buried.

550
00:50:54.099 --> 00:50:56.060
So every night, I dream,

551
00:50:56.101 --> 00:50:57.478
and I go back to that same memory,

552
00:50:57.519 --> 00:50:59.730
and I-I search for details.

553
00:50:59.772 --> 00:51:02.649
For any little thing
that got overlooked.

554
00:51:08.489 --> 00:51:10.032
Yeah.

555
00:51:10.074 --> 00:51:12.576
And that's usually the part
where people tell me I'm crazy.

556
00:51:14.745 --> 00:51:16.789
I know what crazy looks like, Mike.

557
00:51:16.830 --> 00:51:18.749
This isn't it.

558
00:51:18.791 --> 00:51:20.793
Not even close.

559
00:51:21.794 --> 00:51:24.338
And these?

560
00:51:24.380 --> 00:51:26.715
I mean, going back to the same dream,

561
00:51:26.757 --> 00:51:28.425
the same place night after night,

562
00:51:28.467 --> 00:51:31.095
it's not easy,
so the-the pills help.

563
00:51:31.136 --> 00:51:32.346
Some other things,

564
00:51:32.388 --> 00:51:34.264
like familiar sights,
familiar sounds.

565
00:51:34.306 --> 00:51:35.933
"Pining for fun?"

566
00:51:37.518 --> 00:51:39.895
"Visit Nebraska."

567
00:51:39.937 --> 00:51:42.481
Your sister seems cool.

568
00:51:42.523 --> 00:51:45.025
So it's just the two of you?

569
00:51:45.067 --> 00:51:46.902
Yeah.

570
00:51:46.944 --> 00:51:49.446
Yeah, it's just us.

571
00:51:49.488 --> 00:51:52.616
Our mom died a little while back.

572
00:51:53.701 --> 00:51:57.329
And Dad, he couldn't handle it,
so...

573
00:51:59.164 --> 00:52:00.582
You know what's crazy is, uh,

574
00:52:00.624 --> 00:52:02.626
when... when Garrett and I
were kids,

575
00:52:02.668 --> 00:52:05.295
they were like
those perfect parents

576
00:52:05.337 --> 00:52:07.339
you'd see on old TV shows.

577
00:52:09.008 --> 00:52:12.302
Yeah, ev-every night,
we would sit down together,

578
00:52:12.344 --> 00:52:13.846
we'd have family dinner,

579
00:52:13.887 --> 00:52:16.640
and we'd hold hands
and say grace, and...

580
00:52:17.599 --> 00:52:19.393
That actually sounds really nice.

581
00:52:19.435 --> 00:52:24.356
Yeah, at the time,
I thought it was really cheesy.

582
00:52:27.026 --> 00:52:28.944
But then it's gone.

583
00:52:32.573 --> 00:52:36.952
You and Abby,
you still have each other.

584
00:52:38.454 --> 00:52:41.623
From where I sit,
I'd say you're lucky.

585
00:52:46.545 --> 00:52:48.839
I should go.

586
00:52:52.968 --> 00:52:55.471
No more sleeping on the job.

587
00:52:55.512 --> 00:52:58.349
When you're at Freddy's,
you stay alert.

588
00:53:01.602 --> 00:53:03.020
<i>Hey, it's Max.<i>

589
00:53:03.062 --> 00:53:06.148
<i>Leave a message. Or don't.</i>

590
00:53:09.985 --> 00:53:12.237
Come on, Max. Come on.

591
00:53:13.739 --> 00:53:16.241
<i>Hey, it's Max. Leave a mes...</i>

592
00:53:26.168 --> 00:53:27.670
<i>I will work,</i>

593
00:53:27.711 --> 00:53:29.588
and you will sleep,
and under no circumstances

594
00:53:29.630 --> 00:53:30.923
are you gonna come out
of my office.

595
00:53:30.964 --> 00:53:32.800
- Do you understand?
- I understand.

596
00:53:32.841 --> 00:53:36.136
This is not a vacation, okay?
You're not here to have fun.

597
00:53:36.178 --> 00:53:37.721
Okay.

598
00:53:37.763 --> 00:53:39.765
- Whoa, slow down, slow down, slow down.
- No, no, no.

599
00:53:39.807 --> 00:53:40.933
Abby?

600
00:53:47.022 --> 00:53:48.941
Whoa.

601
00:53:48.982 --> 00:53:51.944
What happened?

602
00:53:54.196 --> 00:53:55.864
Give me your hand.

603
00:53:55.906 --> 00:53:57.116
Watch out.

604
00:53:59.034 --> 00:54:02.037
Do you want me
to turn the light off?

605
00:54:03.956 --> 00:54:05.290
Okay.

606
00:54:05.332 --> 00:54:07.292
Good night.

607
00:54:08.544 --> 00:54:10.462
It's like camping.

608
00:56:08.914 --> 00:56:10.749
Abby?

609
00:56:26.098 --> 00:56:28.559
I'll be right back.

610
00:56:41.572 --> 00:56:43.824
Hello?

611
00:56:49.121 --> 00:56:51.457
I know you're back there.

612
00:56:51.498 --> 00:56:53.751
Might as well come out.

613
00:57:21.653 --> 00:57:23.906
You're those kids, right?

614
00:57:28.160 --> 00:57:30.537
The ones who disappeared?

615
00:57:34.667 --> 00:57:36.919
Look.

616
00:57:38.671 --> 00:57:43.258
I don't know how it's possible
that you're here

617
00:57:43.300 --> 00:57:45.678
like this in my dream, but...

618
00:57:48.389 --> 00:57:50.182
...I need your help.

619
00:57:50.224 --> 00:57:52.059
Please.

620
00:57:53.727 --> 00:57:56.271
Help me remember
the man who took my brother.

621
00:58:00.859 --> 00:58:03.320
If we show you,

622
00:58:03.362 --> 00:58:05.197
what will you give us?

623
00:58:06.198 --> 00:58:07.950
Anything.

624
00:58:07.991 --> 00:58:10.202
I'll give you anything you want.

625
00:58:30.180 --> 00:58:31.932
Abby?

626
00:58:35.060 --> 00:58:37.646
Stop! Stop! Stop! <i></i>

627
00:58:37.688 --> 00:58:39.231
Abby?

628
00:58:50.868 --> 00:58:52.411
Mike.

629
00:58:54.163 --> 00:58:55.831
They wouldn't stop tickling me.

630
00:58:55.873 --> 00:58:57.916
I thought I was gonna die.

631
00:58:57.958 --> 00:59:01.712
Freddy, this is my brother, Mike.

632
00:59:04.840 --> 00:59:06.717
- Abby, what is this?
- Come on.

633
00:59:06.759 --> 00:59:08.594
I want you to meet the others.

634
00:59:20.606 --> 00:59:22.900
Mike, this is Bonnie,

635
00:59:22.941 --> 00:59:26.278
Foxy and Chica.

636
00:59:26.320 --> 00:59:29.073
Everyone,

637
00:59:29.114 --> 00:59:30.199
this is Mike.

638
00:59:34.870 --> 00:59:36.538
This-this is a joke, right?

639
00:59:36.580 --> 00:59:38.916
I mean, th-there's someone here.

640
00:59:38.957 --> 00:59:41.710
There's probably somebody
controlling them, right?

641
00:59:41.752 --> 00:59:43.170
I mean...

642
00:59:45.464 --> 00:59:47.424
Okay, good joke!

643
00:59:47.466 --> 00:59:49.510
Congratulations! You got me!

644
00:59:49.551 --> 00:59:51.637
You can come out now!

645
00:59:54.306 --> 00:59:55.641
Hello?

646
01:00:01.772 --> 01:00:03.357
It's okay, Mike.

647
01:00:03.399 --> 01:00:05.275
They just want to play.

648
01:00:08.153 --> 01:00:10.906
- We have to go home now. Come on.
- Hold on.

649
01:00:14.660 --> 01:00:17.121
They really like pictures.

650
01:00:29.591 --> 01:00:32.970
I had a lot of fun tonight.

651
01:00:33.012 --> 01:00:34.805
Thank you for playing with me.

652
01:00:34.847 --> 01:00:38.100
Okay, okay, Abby, come on.

653
01:00:38.142 --> 01:00:39.977
Okay.

654
01:00:49.737 --> 01:00:51.822
Bye!

655
01:01:13.093 --> 01:01:14.720
There you go.

656
01:01:49.505 --> 01:01:51.757
It's them.

657
01:02:09.900 --> 01:02:11.402
Hey, Abby, um,

658
01:02:11.443 --> 01:02:15.155
we need to talk about
last night, okay?

659
01:02:17.199 --> 01:02:18.784
Um...

660
01:02:19.993 --> 01:02:22.913
So those, uh, those...
machines...

661
01:02:22.955 --> 01:02:25.332
My friends?

662
01:02:25.374 --> 01:02:28.335
Your friends?

663
01:02:28.377 --> 01:02:30.421
Um...

664
01:02:30.462 --> 01:02:32.256
are they...?

665
01:02:32.297 --> 01:02:34.508
Ghosts?

666
01:02:34.550 --> 01:02:37.136
- Yeah.
- Of course.

667
01:02:37.177 --> 01:02:40.055
How else could they make
the robots move?

668
01:02:42.516 --> 01:02:44.601
Right.

669
01:02:44.643 --> 01:02:46.311
Can I have some more soup?

670
01:02:48.022 --> 01:02:49.314
Yeah, sure.

671
01:02:53.861 --> 01:02:55.988
Hey, Abs.

672
01:02:56.989 --> 01:02:59.450
You know we used to have
a brother, right?

673
01:03:00.659 --> 01:03:02.369
Garrett.

674
01:03:04.580 --> 01:03:07.958
I don't... I don't really
talk about him very much.

675
01:03:08.000 --> 01:03:10.544
Neither did Mom or Dad.

676
01:03:10.586 --> 01:03:13.088
Yeah, it was hard for them.

677
01:03:13.130 --> 01:03:16.008
It's hard for me, too.

678
01:03:28.270 --> 01:03:31.148
C-Can you explain this to me?

679
01:03:32.524 --> 01:03:35.027
You-you drew that, right?

680
01:03:37.488 --> 01:03:40.491
Okay, and... and-and
you know what that is?

681
01:03:43.619 --> 01:03:44.953
Hey, hey, it's okay.

682
01:03:44.995 --> 01:03:46.497
Okay, I'm not, I'm not mad.

683
01:03:46.538 --> 01:03:48.165
I won't get angry at you.

684
01:03:48.207 --> 01:03:51.293
But I really need you
to help me understand, please.

685
01:03:53.837 --> 01:03:56.882
That's when Garrett got taken.

686
01:03:57.675 --> 01:04:01.261
Abby, who told you about that?

687
01:04:02.513 --> 01:04:05.557
W-Was it a-a boy
with blonde hair?

688
01:04:07.393 --> 01:04:10.896
Did that boy
ever tell you anything

689
01:04:10.938 --> 01:04:13.482
about the man driving that car?

690
01:04:13.524 --> 01:04:15.025
Anything at all?

691
01:04:15.067 --> 01:04:17.444
Okay, just think,
think really hard, okay?

692
01:04:22.825 --> 01:04:24.118
No.

693
01:04:25.619 --> 01:04:28.539
All they talk about
is a yellow rabbit.

694
01:04:29.790 --> 01:04:31.583
Okay.

695
01:04:32.918 --> 01:04:34.503
But...

696
01:04:34.545 --> 01:04:36.046
I can ask.

697
01:04:37.464 --> 01:04:39.925
I would really appreciate that.

698
01:05:05.784 --> 01:05:09.246
<i>♪ We love the yellow rabbit ♪</i>

699
01:05:09.288 --> 01:05:13.083
- <i>♪ We love the yellow rabbit ♪</i>

700
01:05:22.259 --> 01:05:23.844
Vanessa's here.

701
01:05:23.886 --> 01:05:25.179
Yeah.

702
01:05:25.220 --> 01:05:27.431
My friends talk about her sometimes.

703
01:05:27.473 --> 01:05:30.309
- What do they say?
- That she's nice.

704
01:05:30.351 --> 01:05:32.978
Abby, if I asked you
to wait in the car, would you?

705
01:05:33.020 --> 01:05:34.563
No.

706
01:05:35.522 --> 01:05:36.815
Abby, wait.

707
01:05:36.857 --> 01:05:38.317
- Guys, I'm back.
- Abby.

708
01:05:38.359 --> 01:05:41.111
- Hey, Vanessa.
- Abby.

709
01:05:43.322 --> 01:05:46.408
- Mike.
- Vanessa.

710
01:05:46.450 --> 01:05:49.578
I missed you guys.

711
01:05:51.163 --> 01:05:52.998
You knew about this.

712
01:05:56.418 --> 01:05:57.711
Guess you figured it out.

713
01:05:57.753 --> 01:06:00.964
Ghost children possessing giant robots?

714
01:06:01.006 --> 01:06:02.966
Thanks for the heads-up.

715
01:06:03.008 --> 01:06:05.052
Guys, we need help.

716
01:06:08.347 --> 01:06:10.057
It needs to be big

717
01:06:10.099 --> 01:06:12.351
so we can all fit inside.

718
01:06:16.689 --> 01:06:18.857
Abby, look.

719
01:06:18.899 --> 01:06:21.318
Now, this is all really fun
and exciting,

720
01:06:21.360 --> 01:06:23.529
but these things are big,
and they could be dangerous,

721
01:06:23.570 --> 01:06:25.823
so I think we need to lay
some ground rules, all right?

722
01:06:25.864 --> 01:06:27.908
Vanessa, what do you think?

723
01:06:28.992 --> 01:06:32.329
I think we could use the tables
for the fort.

724
01:06:32.371 --> 01:06:35.666
Everyone, follow me.

725
01:06:35.708 --> 01:06:37.584
Come on.

726
01:06:48.137 --> 01:06:50.097
<i>♪ Riding on any wave ♪</i>

727
01:06:50.139 --> 01:06:51.348
<i>♪ That is the luck you crave ♪</i>

728
01:06:51.390 --> 01:06:53.517
<i>♪ They don't believe it now ♪</i>

729
01:06:53.559 --> 01:06:55.394
<i>♪ They just think it's stupid ♪</i>

730
01:06:55.436 --> 01:06:57.855
<i>♪ So got anything? ♪</i>

731
01:06:57.896 --> 01:06:59.940
<i>♪ Anyone could have done ♪</i>

732
01:06:59.982 --> 01:07:01.066
<i>♪ Who would've cared at all... ♪</i>

733
01:07:01.108 --> 01:07:02.901
It needs to be higher.

734
01:07:02.943 --> 01:07:05.029
<i>♪ I don't understand ♪</i>

735
01:07:05.070 --> 01:07:07.489
<i>♪ How a heart is a spade ♪</i>

736
01:07:07.531 --> 01:07:08.782
<i>♪ But somehow the vital ♪</i>

737
01:07:08.824 --> 01:07:10.242
You did it!

738
01:07:10.284 --> 01:07:12.036
<i>♪ Connection is made... ♪</i>

739
01:07:13.620 --> 01:07:15.873
Are you okay?

740
01:07:19.126 --> 01:07:21.295
I like it in here.

741
01:07:21.337 --> 01:07:24.298
Me, too.

742
01:07:24.340 --> 01:07:27.343
But I think it's gonna rain soon.

743
01:07:29.428 --> 01:07:32.181
Sounds like we need a roof.

744
01:07:32.222 --> 01:07:34.391
I'll go see what I can find.

745
01:07:36.352 --> 01:07:38.645
I'll, uh...
I'll-I'll come with you.

746
01:07:39.938 --> 01:07:42.191
Abby, don't forget to ask.

747
01:07:42.232 --> 01:07:44.068
- Okay.
- Yeah.

748
01:07:46.111 --> 01:07:48.072
What are you looking for, exactly?

749
01:07:48.113 --> 01:07:49.865
Tablecloths.

750
01:07:49.907 --> 01:07:52.659
They used to keep 'em back here
for big events.

751
01:07:52.701 --> 01:07:55.746
Right. And remind me how
you know that.

752
01:07:58.791 --> 01:08:00.125
Found 'em.

753
01:08:11.387 --> 01:08:12.429
Don't.

754
01:08:12.471 --> 01:08:14.264
I wouldn't do that.

755
01:08:14.306 --> 01:08:15.724
They're spring locks.

756
01:08:15.766 --> 01:08:17.768
They're on all the older models.

757
01:08:17.810 --> 01:08:19.687
They were designed
to keep the animatronic parts

758
01:08:19.728 --> 01:08:23.649
in place so that, uh, a person
could safely wear the suit.

759
01:08:23.691 --> 01:08:26.694
They tend to be pretty unstable.

760
01:08:26.735 --> 01:08:27.820
Let's see.

761
01:08:29.154 --> 01:08:30.572
Ooh.

762
01:08:32.241 --> 01:08:35.327
Like I said, unstable.

763
01:08:38.288 --> 01:08:40.958
Is there anything else that you
want to tell me about, Vanessa?

764
01:08:41.000 --> 01:08:44.086
'Cause you seem to know
everything about this place.

765
01:08:44.128 --> 01:08:45.170
And what if Abby'd come in here?

766
01:08:45.212 --> 01:08:46.630
What if she'd found that thing?

767
01:08:46.672 --> 01:08:49.466
You're the one who brought her,
Mike, not me.

768
01:08:49.508 --> 01:08:52.511
What I can't wrap
my head around is why.

769
01:08:55.347 --> 01:08:57.516
All right, look.

770
01:08:57.558 --> 01:09:00.853
I think that they know
who took my little brother.

771
01:09:01.687 --> 01:09:03.814
I can't explain it,
but when I'm here,

772
01:09:03.856 --> 01:09:05.274
I feel closer to Garrett.

773
01:09:05.315 --> 01:09:06.817
My dreams are more vivid,
and it...

774
01:09:06.859 --> 01:09:08.819
it's like I can almost...

775
01:09:08.861 --> 01:09:10.863
Change what happened?

776
01:09:17.202 --> 01:09:19.038
Did you ask them about this?

777
01:09:19.079 --> 01:09:20.456
Yeah, I tried.

778
01:09:20.497 --> 01:09:23.709
I don't think
they like me very much.

779
01:09:24.752 --> 01:09:26.211
But...

780
01:09:27.296 --> 01:09:29.673
...they do like Abby.

781
01:09:29.715 --> 01:09:33.010
Mike, you need to drop this.

782
01:09:33.052 --> 01:09:34.887
I don't really see how
that's any of your business.

783
01:09:34.928 --> 01:09:37.890
I'm telling you,
you need to let it go.

784
01:09:38.891 --> 01:09:41.268
Who the hell are you?

785
01:09:42.436 --> 01:09:45.022
Just someone
who's trying to help.

786
01:09:45.064 --> 01:09:47.358
<i>♪ Well, I'm just out of school ♪</i>

787
01:09:47.399 --> 01:09:49.068
<i>♪ Like I'm real, real cool ♪</i>

788
01:09:49.109 --> 01:09:50.611
<i>♪ Got to dance like a fool ♪</i>

789
01:09:50.652 --> 01:09:54.531
<i>♪ Got the message that
I got to be a wild one ♪</i>

790
01:09:54.573 --> 01:09:57.701
<i>♪ Ooh, yeah, I'm a wild one ♪</i>

791
01:09:57.743 --> 01:09:59.036
Vanessa, wait.

792
01:09:59.078 --> 01:10:00.496
<i>♪ Gonna break it loose... ♪</i>

793
01:10:00.537 --> 01:10:02.331
- Talk to me.
- I'm trying.

794
01:10:02.373 --> 01:10:03.665
You're not listening.

795
01:10:03.707 --> 01:10:05.334
Please.
Finding the guy that did this

796
01:10:05.376 --> 01:10:07.086
is the only thing
that matters to me.

797
01:10:11.215 --> 01:10:12.257
Abby?

798
01:10:12.299 --> 01:10:14.677
Wait. Abby, don't!

799
01:10:21.558 --> 01:10:23.268
Abby?

800
01:10:23.310 --> 01:10:26.313
Abby? Abby!

801
01:10:30.984 --> 01:10:34.113
- What happened?
- It's okay, Abby.

802
01:10:34.154 --> 01:10:36.073
You just had an accident.

803
01:10:36.115 --> 01:10:38.409
You're okay.

804
01:10:41.203 --> 01:10:43.330
I'm so sorry.

805
01:10:47.626 --> 01:10:50.421
I don't know what to say.

806
01:10:50.462 --> 01:10:53.048
Just go home, Mike.

807
01:10:53.090 --> 01:10:54.633
Take care of your sister.

808
01:10:56.427 --> 01:10:58.971
What are you so afraid of?

809
01:11:00.305 --> 01:11:02.683
In the storage room...

810
01:11:02.725 --> 01:11:05.477
I saw your eyes.
You were terrified.

811
01:11:11.275 --> 01:11:13.444
You can do whatever you want
with your own life,

812
01:11:13.485 --> 01:11:16.030
but if you ever bring Abby
back here again,

813
01:11:16.071 --> 01:11:18.323
I will shoot you.

814
01:11:27.666 --> 01:11:30.127
She looked so angry.

815
01:11:30.169 --> 01:11:33.964
Why does everyone always
look at you that way?

816
01:11:53.692 --> 01:11:56.320
Hey, it's Mike.

817
01:11:56.362 --> 01:11:58.322
I need your help.

818
01:12:10.334 --> 01:12:11.960
Abby.

819
01:12:12.920 --> 01:12:14.713
Is that bacon?

820
01:12:14.755 --> 01:12:16.006
Hey, why don't you, uh, get dressed

821
01:12:16.048 --> 01:12:17.508
and then come to the kitchen, okay?

822
01:12:17.549 --> 01:12:18.967
I want to talk to you
about something.

823
01:12:19.009 --> 01:12:20.636
Okay.

824
01:12:25.766 --> 01:12:29.061
Wow, there's my favorite
little girl.

825
01:12:30.604 --> 01:12:32.398
Come have a seat, all right?

826
01:12:33.190 --> 01:12:34.858
What did you do?

827
01:12:34.900 --> 01:12:36.652
Abby, look, I think
if you just sit down,

828
01:12:36.694 --> 01:12:38.862
we can explain it to you, okay?

829
01:12:38.904 --> 01:12:40.197
No.

830
01:12:40.239 --> 01:12:42.616
I promise you, this is not
what you think it is.

831
01:12:42.658 --> 01:12:45.369
I hate you.

832
01:12:45.411 --> 01:12:47.579
I hate you, Mike!

833
01:12:50.958 --> 01:12:53.836
Well, I-I think that went well.

834
01:13:06.682 --> 01:13:08.684
She reminds me of you, you know.

835
01:13:08.726 --> 01:13:11.395
Always with the temper.

836
01:13:11.437 --> 01:13:12.688
Well, look, when she calms down,

837
01:13:12.730 --> 01:13:14.481
can you, um, tell her that I'm sorry

838
01:13:14.523 --> 01:13:17.151
and that I'll-I'll be back soon?

839
01:13:17.192 --> 01:13:21.196
Well, Mike,
there's a larger conversation

840
01:13:21.238 --> 01:13:23.115
that needs to happen here.

841
01:13:23.157 --> 01:13:25.492
So when you do get back,
you and me are gonna have

842
01:13:25.534 --> 01:13:27.161
a little chat.

843
01:13:27.202 --> 01:13:29.121
Okay.

844
01:13:35.294 --> 01:13:38.130
<i>♪ Celebrate good times, come on ♪</i>

845
01:13:40.924 --> 01:13:42.926
<i>♪ Let's celebrate ♪</i>

846
01:13:42.968 --> 01:13:44.762
<i>♪ Celebrate good times... ♪</i>

847
01:13:44.803 --> 01:13:47.014
You know what works for me?

848
01:13:47.056 --> 01:13:50.059
A warm glass of milk
with chamomile and honey.

849
01:13:50.100 --> 01:13:51.935
I tell you...

850
01:13:54.438 --> 01:13:56.648
What an asshole.

851
01:14:50.953 --> 01:14:53.080
Okay, enough games, you two.

852
01:14:53.122 --> 01:14:54.748
Emergency landing.

853
01:14:54.790 --> 01:14:56.583
Coming in.

854
01:14:56.625 --> 01:14:58.752
Hey, buddy.

855
01:14:59.837 --> 01:15:01.463
Well, don't just stand there.
Dig in.

856
01:15:06.969 --> 01:15:08.971
Sweetheart, what's wrong?

857
01:15:09.930 --> 01:15:12.725
This... this isn't...

858
01:15:12.766 --> 01:15:15.019
this isn't how it happened.

859
01:15:16.061 --> 01:15:17.521
This isn't real.

860
01:15:17.563 --> 01:15:19.023
But it could be.

861
01:15:20.315 --> 01:15:22.860
What is this?

862
01:15:22.901 --> 01:15:24.528
This isn't what I asked for.

863
01:15:24.570 --> 01:15:26.822
But it's what you want.

864
01:15:26.864 --> 01:15:30.367
No. I just, I just want
to find the man that...

865
01:15:30.409 --> 01:15:31.702
You're lying.

866
01:15:31.744 --> 01:15:33.704
You want to save Garrett.

867
01:15:33.746 --> 01:15:35.664
That's why you're really here.

868
01:15:35.706 --> 01:15:38.167
To change what happened.

869
01:15:38.208 --> 01:15:39.626
To go back.

870
01:15:39.668 --> 01:15:41.754
But I can't.

871
01:15:42.963 --> 01:15:44.590
He's gone. They're all gone.

872
01:15:44.631 --> 01:15:46.759
Really?

873
01:15:54.808 --> 01:15:58.645
You can have this dream every night.

874
01:15:58.687 --> 01:16:00.647
You can be together
with him again.

875
01:16:00.689 --> 01:16:03.233
Like before.

876
01:16:03.275 --> 01:16:04.985
How?

877
01:16:05.027 --> 01:16:08.614
You said we could have
anything we wanted.

878
01:16:09.406 --> 01:16:13.285
We want Abby.

879
01:16:15.454 --> 01:16:17.331
Abby?

880
01:16:21.001 --> 01:16:25.172
They love her, Mike,
and she loves them.

881
01:16:27.132 --> 01:16:29.426
You've seen her with them.

882
01:16:29.468 --> 01:16:32.179
You've seen how happy she is.

883
01:16:34.890 --> 01:16:38.268
It's time to let her go, sweetheart.

884
01:16:38.310 --> 01:16:42.147
You were never the right person
to take care of her.

885
01:16:54.326 --> 01:16:56.954
Okay.

886
01:17:00.833 --> 01:17:02.918
Yes.

887
01:17:07.673 --> 01:17:09.758
You're home.

888
01:17:24.815 --> 01:17:27.026
No.

889
01:17:28.736 --> 01:17:30.362
No, this is wrong.

890
01:17:30.404 --> 01:17:33.198
I don't, I don't want this.
Listen...

891
01:17:45.794 --> 01:17:48.047
I made a mistake!

892
01:17:48.088 --> 01:17:50.591
Please, I don't want this!

893
01:17:50.632 --> 01:17:52.301
Do you hear me?!

894
01:17:55.679 --> 01:17:57.639
You leave Abby alone!

895
01:18:02.644 --> 01:18:04.521
Abby.

896
01:18:04.563 --> 01:18:06.106
Abby.

897
01:18:06.148 --> 01:18:08.442
Stay away from my sister!

898
01:18:12.821 --> 01:18:14.406
Abby.

899
01:18:15.866 --> 01:18:17.868
- Abby.
- Abby.

900
01:18:22.122 --> 01:18:23.832
Abby.

901
01:18:27.002 --> 01:18:29.380
Abby. Abby.

902
01:18:29.421 --> 01:18:32.299
Abby. Abby. Abby.

903
01:18:36.095 --> 01:18:38.305
Abby.

904
01:19:50.878 --> 01:19:53.505
No!

905
01:20:00.137 --> 01:20:02.306
Abby?

906
01:20:02.348 --> 01:20:05.351
You can't stay in there
forever, you know.

907
01:20:10.397 --> 01:20:11.899
Suit yourself.

908
01:20:21.200 --> 01:20:22.659
The pottery that grows.

909
01:20:22.701 --> 01:20:24.078
<i>It's easy.</i>

910
01:20:24.119 --> 01:20:25.871
<i>Soak your Chia overnight,
spread the seeds...</i>

911
01:20:27.206 --> 01:20:29.416
Oh.

912
01:20:44.598 --> 01:20:45.683
Freddy?

913
01:20:53.065 --> 01:20:55.526
Not Freddy.

914
01:20:57.111 --> 01:20:59.697
They're all waiting for you.

915
01:20:59.738 --> 01:21:01.323
It's time to go play.

916
01:21:08.872 --> 01:21:11.041
Silly Aunt Jane.

917
01:21:11.083 --> 01:21:12.584
She fell asleep.

918
01:21:15.087 --> 01:21:16.714
How do we get there?

919
01:21:18.924 --> 01:21:20.676
<i>♪ I wanna be down ♪</i>

920
01:21:20.718 --> 01:21:23.095
<i>♪ With what you're going through ♪</i>

921
01:21:23.137 --> 01:21:25.889
<i>♪ I wanna be down... ♪</i>

922
01:21:25.931 --> 01:21:28.267
Where to, little lady?

923
01:21:30.811 --> 01:21:32.271
What the...?

924
01:21:32.813 --> 01:21:34.606
Oh, my goodness!

925
01:21:38.610 --> 01:21:40.279
Not cool.

926
01:21:40.320 --> 01:21:43.032
Why do I always get the weirdos?

927
01:21:57.338 --> 01:21:58.964
Careful.

928
01:21:59.006 --> 01:22:01.342
I managed to stop the bleeding,

929
01:22:01.383 --> 01:22:03.427
but you're probably
gonna need stitches.

930
01:22:03.469 --> 01:22:05.012
Where are we?

931
01:22:05.054 --> 01:22:07.306
Police supply outpost.

932
01:22:07.348 --> 01:22:11.894
I found you,
and, uh, you were...

933
01:22:11.935 --> 01:22:13.562
you were badly hurt.

934
01:22:16.315 --> 01:22:19.109
They tried to kill me, Vanessa.

935
01:22:21.320 --> 01:22:24.156
But I'm guessing
you already knew that.

936
01:22:28.077 --> 01:22:29.661
Max.

937
01:22:30.829 --> 01:22:32.289
Her brother.

938
01:22:32.331 --> 01:22:34.833
You knew about them, too, right?

939
01:22:35.584 --> 01:22:38.045
- It's complicated.
- Yeah.

940
01:22:38.087 --> 01:22:39.880
Yeah.

941
01:22:39.922 --> 01:22:42.049
More complicated than

942
01:22:42.091 --> 01:22:44.009
possessed robots
murdering innocent people?

943
01:22:44.051 --> 01:22:45.969
They weren't innocent.

944
01:22:46.011 --> 01:22:47.471
Yeah, Abby is!

945
01:22:48.305 --> 01:22:51.225
- Mike...
- You saw Abby playing with them.

946
01:22:51.266 --> 01:22:52.810
And you knew
what they were capable of,

947
01:22:52.851 --> 01:22:54.978
- and you didn't say anything!
- Mike, please just...

948
01:22:55.020 --> 01:22:56.689
Abby is in danger!

949
01:22:56.730 --> 01:22:59.358
Tell me what happened.

950
01:23:01.568 --> 01:23:03.404
In my dream...

951
01:23:04.905 --> 01:23:07.741
...they asked me for Abby.

952
01:23:07.783 --> 01:23:09.493
And I said yes.

953
01:23:10.536 --> 01:23:14.123
It was a mistake,
and I-I tried to fix it, but...

954
01:23:15.958 --> 01:23:18.669
What do they want
with my sister?

955
01:23:21.213 --> 01:23:24.633
They want to make her like them.

956
01:23:34.393 --> 01:23:36.729
Come on, let's go.

957
01:23:49.992 --> 01:23:52.244
Where'd you go?

958
01:23:57.458 --> 01:24:01.754
<i>In the '80s,</i>
<i>when those kids went missing...</i>

959
01:24:02.588 --> 01:24:04.881
...the police searched Freddy's
from top to bottom.

960
01:24:04.923 --> 01:24:08.260
Every inch was accounted for.

961
01:24:09.928 --> 01:24:12.264
<i>But they never found them.</i>

962
01:24:18.979 --> 01:24:20.731
Hello?

963
01:24:25.194 --> 01:24:26.904
<i>The man who took them,</i>

964
01:24:26.945 --> 01:24:28.781
<i>he was a...</i>

965
01:24:30.449 --> 01:24:33.118
<i>He was a very bad man.</i>

966
01:24:33.911 --> 01:24:36.663
A very cruel man.

967
01:24:37.539 --> 01:24:40.376
Also a very clever man.

968
01:24:40.417 --> 01:24:42.252
<i>He knew that parents would cry,</i>

969
01:24:42.294 --> 01:24:43.962
<i>and the police</i>
<i>would come looking.</i>

970
01:24:44.004 --> 01:24:45.798
<i>And he knew there's one place</i>

971
01:24:45.839 --> 01:24:48.550
- <i>they'd never think to check because...</i>
- <i></i>

972
01:24:50.344 --> 01:24:52.179
...why would they?

973
01:24:55.474 --> 01:24:57.643
<i>I mean, why would anyone?</i>

974
01:25:05.651 --> 01:25:10.155
It's not just their ghosts that
are inside of those machines.

975
01:25:16.120 --> 01:25:18.372
It's their bodies.

976
01:25:20.249 --> 01:25:23.293
You have to understand, the...

977
01:25:23.335 --> 01:25:26.130
the kids, they don't want
to hurt anyone.

978
01:25:26.171 --> 01:25:27.381
It's-it's him.

979
01:25:27.423 --> 01:25:30.592
He influences them somehow.

980
01:25:30.634 --> 01:25:34.847
He took everything from them,
but they don't remember.

981
01:25:34.888 --> 01:25:37.391
Who, Vanessa?

982
01:25:37.433 --> 01:25:40.227
I tried to warn you.

983
01:25:40.269 --> 01:25:43.355
I really did try in my own way.

984
01:25:44.273 --> 01:25:45.607
But it's too late now.

985
01:25:45.649 --> 01:25:47.901
He knows that
you're looking for him.

986
01:25:49.903 --> 01:25:52.072
He'll be coming.

987
01:25:52.114 --> 01:25:56.702
You need to tell me who he is.

988
01:26:04.209 --> 01:26:08.714
His name is William Afton.

989
01:26:11.383 --> 01:26:13.886
He's my father.

990
01:26:32.738 --> 01:26:34.948
You knew?

991
01:26:34.990 --> 01:26:36.367
Mike...

992
01:26:36.408 --> 01:26:38.202
This whole time.

993
01:26:38.243 --> 01:26:40.079
My brother, you knew.

994
01:26:40.120 --> 01:26:42.206
Not about Garrett, no.

995
01:26:42.247 --> 01:26:44.875
A-At least...

996
01:26:44.917 --> 01:26:46.418
not when we met.

997
01:26:50.964 --> 01:26:53.050
I'm so, so sorry.

998
01:26:53.092 --> 01:26:55.010
Tell me how to stop them.

999
01:26:55.052 --> 01:26:56.929
Tell me how to save my sister!

1000
01:27:12.027 --> 01:27:14.947
Electricity.
Electricity is the key.

1001
01:27:16.115 --> 01:27:19.326
We use these for animal control.

1002
01:27:21.120 --> 01:27:22.663
There's a Taser on your belt.

1003
01:27:22.705 --> 01:27:24.748
It won't do permanent damage,

1004
01:27:24.790 --> 01:27:27.251
but it'll mess with
the animatronic circuitry.

1005
01:27:27.292 --> 01:27:28.794
Hopefully buy you some time.

1006
01:27:30.295 --> 01:27:32.548
Come with me.

1007
01:27:33.340 --> 01:27:35.092
No.

1008
01:27:35.134 --> 01:27:38.804
Vanessa, you owe it to me,
and you owe it to them.

1009
01:27:38.846 --> 01:27:40.431
No, I can't.

1010
01:27:40.472 --> 01:27:42.474
If he's there, I...

1011
01:27:43.475 --> 01:27:46.687
...I won't be any use to you,
believe me.

1012
01:27:48.981 --> 01:27:51.483
He really messed you up,
didn't he?

1013
01:27:56.947 --> 01:27:58.782
Take these.

1014
01:28:10.044 --> 01:28:12.629
<i>You need to avoid</i>
<i>the front entrance.</i>

1015
01:28:20.596 --> 01:28:21.972
<i>There's an outlet vent</i>

1016
01:28:22.014 --> 01:28:23.390
<i>on the east side of the building.</i>

1017
01:28:23.432 --> 01:28:25.893
<i>That's the best way inside.</i>

1018
01:28:41.200 --> 01:28:42.526
<i>♪ You tell me that you want me ♪</i>

1019
01:28:42.568 --> 01:28:44.278
<i></i> No.

1020
01:28:44.620 --> 01:28:46.872
<i>♪ You tell me that you need me ♪</i>

1021
01:28:48.624 --> 01:28:51.835
<i>♪ You tell me that you love me ♪</i>

1022
01:28:51.877 --> 01:28:54.088
<i>♪ And I know that I'm right ♪</i>

1023
01:28:54.129 --> 01:28:55.881
<i>♪ 'Cause I hear it in the night ♪</i>

1024
01:28:55.923 --> 01:29:00.094
<i>♪ I hear the secrets that you keep... ♪</i>

1025
01:29:03.889 --> 01:29:07.142
<i>♪ I hear the secrets that you keep... ♪</i>

1026
01:29:18.028 --> 01:29:19.822
<i>♪ Don't you know you're sleeping... ♪</i>

1027
01:29:31.333 --> 01:29:32.584
Abby.

1028
01:29:41.927 --> 01:29:44.555
Chica, where are we going?

1029
01:29:52.604 --> 01:29:54.023
<i>♪ And I know that I'm right ♪</i>

1030
01:29:54.064 --> 01:29:56.900
<i>♪ 'Cause I hear it in the night ♪</i>

1031
01:29:56.942 --> 01:30:01.030
<i>♪ I hear the secrets that you keep ♪</i>

1032
01:30:01.071 --> 01:30:03.073
<i>♪ When you're talking in your sleep ♪</i>

1033
01:30:16.295 --> 01:30:20.049
Chica, I don't like this.

1034
01:30:25.471 --> 01:30:27.556
Let go of me!

1035
01:30:27.698 --> 01:30:28.757
Abby?!

1036
01:30:32.478 --> 01:30:33.937
Chica, let me go.

1037
01:30:33.979 --> 01:30:35.731
Hey!

1038
01:30:38.692 --> 01:30:39.985
Leave her alone!

1039
01:30:51.288 --> 01:30:52.331
Mike.

1040
01:30:52.373 --> 01:30:53.791
Hey.

1041
01:30:53.832 --> 01:30:55.125
Are you okay? Are you hurt?

1042
01:30:55.167 --> 01:30:56.919
I don't know what's wrong with her.

1043
01:30:56.960 --> 01:30:59.004
I don't know why she was
trying to hurt me.

1044
01:30:59.046 --> 01:31:01.173
I know. I know.

1045
01:31:01.215 --> 01:31:03.634
Hey, Abby, listen to me.

1046
01:31:03.676 --> 01:31:06.887
I've been an idiot
about so many things.

1047
01:31:06.929 --> 01:31:09.139
I've been stuck
trying to fix the past,

1048
01:31:09.181 --> 01:31:11.934
but you are the most important
thing in the world to me,

1049
01:31:11.975 --> 01:31:13.644
and I promise you
I'm gonna do better.

1050
01:31:13.686 --> 01:31:15.562
I love you, too, Mike.

1051
01:31:15.604 --> 01:31:17.314
But we should probably go now.

1052
01:31:17.356 --> 01:31:18.857
Right, okay. Come on.

1053
01:31:37.292 --> 01:31:39.003
Mike!

1054
01:31:40.504 --> 01:31:42.506
Run! Hide! Abby, go!

1055
01:33:21.772 --> 01:33:23.607
Abby?

1056
01:33:23.649 --> 01:33:25.818
Abby, where are you?

1057
01:33:28.821 --> 01:33:30.114
Abby?

1058
01:34:32.593 --> 01:34:33.719
- Vanessa.
